    <DataNode elementId="AT1G27450-MONOMER" textLabel="adenine phosphoribosyltransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT1G27450-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="335" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The Arabidopsis genome has five adenine phosphoribosyltransferase sequences. APT1, APT2 and APT3 have been cloned, over-expressed, and their catalytic properties characterized. All three isozymes bind adenine efficiently. APT1 is 42-80 times more efficient, judged by Vmax/Km, in metabolizing adenine than that of APT2 and APT3. The three isozymes also metabolize cytokinins. The kinetic properties of the three isozymes suggest they contribute primarily in adenine salvage.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G27450-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-12203" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G27450.3" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G27450" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="28." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="28." />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12010467" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT5G18860-MONOMER" textLabel="purine nucleoside hydrolase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT5G18860-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="335" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">|FRAME: AT5G18860| is a extracellular purine nucleosidase that appears to catalyze the hydrolysis of |FRAME: INOSINE| and |FRAME: ADENOSINE| |CITS: [21235647][14595688][15769804]|. Although its function has not been confirmed through &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; assays, the inosine and adenosine hydrolase activities observed in the |FRAME: ORG-5993| apoplast are almost completely lost in plants lacking NSH3. The enzymatic activity observed in wild type apoplasts yielded a tenfold lower maximal catalytic activity with |FRAME: ADENOSINE| than with |FRAME: INOSINE|. Nevertheless, NSH3 may be involved in the salvage of extracellular adenosine created through extracellular ATP signaling. Consistent with that hypothesis, |FRAME: AT5G18860| transcript levels rise in response to |FRAME: Jasmonic-Acids jasmonic acid| and wounding, two stimuli that may be linked to extracellular purine metabolism |CITS: [21235647]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G18860-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="purine hydrolase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="purine nucleosidase" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33938, RXN-12887, RXN-12888" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="3" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005576, GO:0009505" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G18860.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G18860" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="15769804, 14595688" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-EXTRACELLULAR-PL, CCO-CW-PLANT" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_21235647" />
    </DataNode>
